WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.875
Gap three is narrower.

2
00:00:01.875 --> 00:00:06.225
Identity Security Cloud's Service
Desk integration creates service

3
00:00:06.225 --> 00:00:09.975
requests and incidents only; it
can't create change requests.

4
00:00:09.975 --> 00:00:11.650
IdentityIQ's can.

5
00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:14.387
So where a change class
needs a change record,

6
00:00:14.387 --> 00:00:17.125
a ServiceNow flow raises
it from the request.

7
00:00:17.125 --> 00:00:19.875
Gap four is about who
writes to the directory.

8
00:00:19.875 --> 00:00:24.967
SailPoint reads Oracle HCM Cloud
directly and writes back only user

9
00:00:24.967 --> 00:00:30.238
name and work email, which fits the
workbook's HR-driven identity design.

10
00:00:30.238 --> 00:00:35.201
But that design makes Entra inbound
provisioning the one writer into the directory.

11
00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:37.312
So pick one writer per attribute.

12
00:00:37.312 --> 00:00:42.078
Either inbound provisioning stays the
door and SailPoint governs entitlements,

13
00:00:42.078 --> 00:00:44.812
or SailPoint takes on
the provisioning duties.

14
00:00:44.812 --> 00:00:45.787
Not both.

15
00:00:45.787 --> 00:00:47.860
Now, the identity fixes.
